{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/172131-hedge-creatures-outside-of-the-hedge-question","id":172131,"title":"Hedge creatures outside of the hedge question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-17T16:19:25-07:00","id":172131,"title":"Hedge creatures outside of the hedge question","content":"Hello!<br /> <br /> I've been in a game or two where Hobs kind of melt when they leave the hedge and are seen by normal people. When snooping around to learn the game better, I didn't come across this in the books (Or if I did, I was probably a little sleepy so it didn't stick in my head).<br /> <br /> Did I overlook the spot? Or is it in a spot I haven't looked yet? Book and page number would be great, but just knowing where to look would be fantastic~","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/287-wildfire","name":"Wildfire","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T17:33:46-07:00","id":172202,"title":"","content":"There's no actual rule for it. Some Hobgoblins (Bunyips, Border Reavers, and possibly Drudgemen just from the top of my head) only work as written if they can leave the Hedge. Mechanically speaking, there's no reason a Hobgoblin can't go anywhere they want. Hobgoblins are exceptionally diverse with their own unique abilities though, and it wouldn't be impossible for certain species to do as you describe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T17:36:31-07:00","id":172208,"title":"","content":"Autumn Nightmares covers it a little, but it basically comes down to some would love to go, some would freak out and want to go back to the hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T17:57:20-07:00","id":172219,"title":"","content":"Not to mention that some Goblin Markets are outside of the Hedge, so Hobs not being able to leave wouldn't make much sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T21:59:23-07:00","id":172439,"title":"","content":"Some hobs suffer when they leave the hedge though, so yeah it really depends on the hob.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T22:15:25-07:00","id":172453,"title":"","content":"In our changeling game a hobgoblin stumbled out of the hedge and into a couple would-be hunters who then became hunters and made our game awkward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-18T10:48:17-07:00","id":172966,"title":"","content":"I've found vampires, among all the other splats, to be well-suited to adaptation as a type of hobgoblin (or severed Fae wisp) that has become permanently adapted to Earthly existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/486-foolish-milex","name":"Foolish Milex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T06:26:39-07:00","id":174037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Foolish Milex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/172131-hedge-creatures-outside-of-the-hedge-question?p=172966#post172966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've found vampires, among all the other splats, to be well-suited to adaptation as a type of hobgoblin (or severed Fae wisp) that has become permanently adapted to Earthly existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>It that why the hedge is so vicious with them? Some kind of anger over their leaving?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2002-quynce","name":"Quynce","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2002_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T08:02:54-07:00","id":174137,"title":"","content":"It doesn't seem that bad to me, as long as they know how to follow Nighted Trods, but they've long since lost their intuitions and mutated away from a glamoured-blood-drinking (necro-)metabolism to a messier one that runs on human blood and spiritedness. The Thorns can't soak it up anymore, but it can still cut them and generate a faint, but obnoxious pull on their Vitae. Of course, since they're being reduced to be one small fragment of a Changeling-focused setting, all their Covenants and history are dropped and their Blood Potency is capped at 5. P= Their undead traits shouldn't be too out of line for hobgoblins from the gothic bits of the Hedge, and their mind-focused powers recall the emotional aspects of Glamour and help them be notable manipulators of Changeling courts, which is a role usually reserved for other Changelings and the occasional True Fae or Goblin Market.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/486-foolish-milex","name":"Foolish Milex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar486_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-19T21:51:14-07:00","id":174949,"title":"","content":"Ive use hobgobs outside of the hedge before but i haven't really used them existing outside of it for long, mostly in pursuit of the characters or summoned via loyalists who have made bargains with the true Fae for trinkets that would do so.<br /> <br /> But all in all i see not problem with them exiting the hedge but like mentioned before i dont think there is much motivation for them to stay here , i mean our world is way to boring compared to the dynamic life within the hedge for a hobo(in my opinion anyway,though i would agree with any story if it suited the setting).<br /> <br /> i would say all in all to treat hobo's by there motivations, if it suits them fine to be in the real world id do so, but how long they can stay and what long term effect it has on them is up to the storyteller.<br /> <br /> What would be cool is having something similar happening to a hobo that happens to the gentry if there here for to long, wonder what a hob would be like suddenly becoming a changeling.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1951-themoetan","name":"TheMoetan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1951_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-20T06:03:59-07:00","id":175174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheMoetan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/172131-hedge-creatures-outside-of-the-hedge-question?p=174949#post174949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would be cool is having something similar happening to a hobo that happens to the gentry if there here for to long, wonder what a hob would be like suddenly becoming a changeling.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah. Pretty much my favourite character from Grim Fears was the Hobgoblin spider who became what she ate. And so, when she devoured one of the gentry, she was suddenly elevated into this considerably more powerful and intelligent being. A similar version skewed more towards gaining humanity would be amazing.<br /> <br /> Gives me ideas for a Changeling-based Promethean as well...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}